ller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own comment says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). The test checks that 2.665 rounds to 2.66, so it failed.\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit 08d3cd5986 passed.\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 to confirm the requirement, but the advisory system didn't recognize that ID. I went by the test and the code comment, which agree with each other.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}